Good point. I optimized it by using a single query with a LEFT JOIN on roles and permissions. Also added a B-tree index on `users.email`. Here's the updated code:

```javascript
const getUserWithRoles = async (email) => {
  return db('users')
    .select('users.*', 'roles.name as role_name', 'permissions.name as permission_name')
    .leftJoin('roles', 'users.role_id', 'roles.id')
    .leftJoin('permissions', 'roles.permission_id', 'permissions.id')
    .where('users.email', email);
};
```

Login time dropped from 2.8s to 120ms (P99).

